---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-08-29';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'August 29, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <p>{APP_NAME} is published by {BUSINESS_NAME}.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} sends analytics to <SiteLink href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/" target="_blank" aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab">TelemetryDeck</SiteLink>. This data includes app use,
      purchases, crashes, performance, app and device information, a random
      identifier for each install, and settings such as accessibility, color
      scheme, language, layout direction, and region. {APP_NAME} uses it to
      improve the app.
    </p>
    <p>
      When analytics are turned off in the app's settings, no more data is sent.
      Earlier records are not deleted, and there is no set date for their
      removal. They have no name, email, or other detail tied to a person, so
      one person's records cannot be found and deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      TelemetryDeck must protect this data at least as well as this policy and
      Apple's rules require.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Content reports</h2>
    <p>
      A content report is an email that includes the reason, round ID, app
      version, build number, and the reporter's email address. The drawing is
      included only if the reporter attaches it. {BUSINESS_NAME} uses the report
      to review the content.
    </p>
    <p>
      Report emails stay in the support inbox. One can be removed by emailing <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> from the address that sent it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      No one uses {APP_NAME} to track activity on other websites or in other
      companies' apps.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>Important changes to this policy are posted here.</p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time>.</footer>
</Doc>
